#### February

I did find out that `DataInputStream.readUTF()` was completely broken after
reading single byte characters across `read()` barriers. Such barrier is hit
when two characters are attempted to be read for a multibyte character, however
there is no character yet available in the input stream. This is a fix to
old code from 2018.

ScritchUI got some buffer overflow fixes, which is always good. There also
were improvements cherry-picked from `wip-cocoa`, which as of
today (October 2026) is still around in a branch. Graphics can also be closed.

A very important thing however is `wip-serialpen` which is exactly what it says
on the tin. It serialized ScritchPencil, effectively meaning that it is now
part of the ScritchUI event loop and drawing is inlined and correct for the
most part. It is effectively how OpenGL and such operate, so whenever that
happens it will be ready for it.

There was also module cleanup and refactoring, I started prefixing modules
so that SquirrelJME specific libraries that are not SquirrelJME Runtime
specific, but can be used by anyone, are prefixed by `vendor-api-squirreljme-`.

Then `wip-nanocoatexec` continued along. More instructions were implemented
such as invoking methods and loading variables. Command line parsing started
to get implemented. Much of the basis for the stack was implemented as well.
Of course later on, how stacks work would be redone. The very basis for
MLE calls also started being a thing as well.

The JSON library, from before SquirrelJME even existed (!) from 2014, got
more methods implemented along with a refactor to support base Java ME so it
could be used internally.

There were additionally a number of compiler specific checks and fixes for
all the various environment configurations. Along with the very primitive
basis for CMake patching.

