> ScritchPencilRasterShapes: Move arc drawing code to fixed-point. The hardware
> float guards were removed entirely from there as all architectures can use
> these now. drawArc got some optimizations bundled in by the means of DDA
> usage so that sin/cos is no longer calculated for each step, and fillArc,
> which was the biggest bottleneck previously, got swapped to a scanline
> algorithm that runs orders of magnitude faster while also dropping the need
> for that temporary "alpha buffer". As a bonus, some extra FP functions were
> also implemented. Not all of them are needed for arc drawing, but it's good
> to have them there for whenever something actually does.
> 
> DoJa: Update Graphics, Image, and Sprite classes. ImageMap and Sprites were
> initially introduced as optional packages in DoJa, but as of DoJa 3.5, they
> were made part of the core specification, going from 'opt.ui' to 'ui'. This
> commit implements them as their newer versions. What this means is that
> opt.ui.Graphics2 should now link its SpriteSet and ImageMap drawing methods
> to ui.Graphics, and the older opt.ui versions of SpriteSet and ImageMap
> should be redirected to their ui equivalents now. A few methods in Graphics2,
> Graphics and Image were also implemented based on their specifications, with
